-- title:
--   A good off-branch point reading each non-node Igusa place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $5 \le q$ and a level $M'$ with $M' \neq 0$ and $q \nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense of `LiesOverPrime`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` over `ResidueField A` which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)`: the rational affine geometric places $w$ whose value $w.\mathrm{evalAt}$ at the generator `jGeomGen` lies in `ssJSet q (ResidueField A)` (the set of $j$ such that every elliptic curve with that invariant has no nonzero $q$-torsion point). Let `hle` record the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'` of the base-changed full modular function field into the geometric function field of level $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, and let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective residue map with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ on constants, together with the place map and the order-preservation clauses of that structure). The hypothesis `hR₀` states that for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, this element lies in `R₀.integers` and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over `ResidueField A`, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   Let $\zeta$ be an element of `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$), and let $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ assign a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each point of the projective line [`CuspidalType.ProjLine q`](def/CuspidalType_IsCuspidalOfType.html#L21) over $\mathbb{Z}/q$, and $O_{\mathrm{SS}}$ a valuation subring of `fieldBar q M'` to each $s \in W$.
--
--   The Igusa group of hypotheses: `hIg_inf` describes $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ as a Gauss-type ring, namely $f$ belongs to it precisely when there are Laurent series $x, y$ over $A$ with the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ nonzero and $f \cdot y = x$ in `LaurentSeries (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`; `hIg` says every line $\ell$ is of the form $\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma \cdot \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ for some $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ with $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ the pullback of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ along `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ`; `hIg_inj` asserts injectivity of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$; `hIg_perm` asserts that for each `ζ' : Idx q` and each $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` permutes the family $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}$.
--
--   The supersingular group: `hSS_A` says that for each $s$ a constant $x \in \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ exactly when $x \in A$; `hSS_over` says that for $s \in W$ and $f \in$ `R₀.integers` whose order is non-negative at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the base-changed $j$-invariant `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq` has non-negative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$, and moreover for every $a \in A$ whose residue equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $f$, the difference of that image and $a$ lies in the maximal ideal of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$; `hSS_fix` says each $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ is invariant under pullback along `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; `hSS_tr` provides for each $s$ an element $t \in O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ with $t - a$ a unit of $O_{\mathrm{SS}}(s)$ for every $a \in A$.
--
--   The prolongation group: $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` with `R.integers` equal to $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$ (`hR`), and `hR₀O` says that $f$ lies in `R₀.integers` exactly when its image in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\mathrm{lineInfty}\,q)$.
--
--   The arithmetic group: $\pi \in A$ with $\pi^{q^2-1} = q$; an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ such that $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`) and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`), together with `hκ`: every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Further, an auxiliary prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{q^2-1} = q \cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$. Finally $K_1$ is a finite extension of $k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $A_1$ a valuation subring of $K_1$ cut out by $A$ (`hA₁`), assumed a henselian discrete valuation ring.
--
--   With `fieldBar q M'` given its $k_0$-algebra structure through $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the conclusion quantifies over every intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ subject to four conditions: the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by all constants is everything; $F_0$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ' γ` for all `ζ'` and all $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; a linear disjointness condition, namely for every finite extension $K'$ of $k_0$ in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, every $m$, every $K'$-linearly independent family $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and every family $a$ of elements of the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces $a_i = 0$ for all $i$; and $F_0$ contains every element of `fieldBar q M'` whose Laurent series lies in the range of `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`.
--
--   Write $T_1$ for the compositum `IntermediateField.adjoin ↥k₀ (algebraMap (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) ↥(fieldBar q M') '' K₁) ⊔ F₀`. The statement then quantifies over an $A_1$-algebra structure on $T_1$ whose structure map is compatible with the inclusions of $A_1 \subseteq K_1 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ into `fieldBar q M'`, over an element $j_1 \in T_1$ whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is the image under `hle` of the base-changed $j$-invariant `coeffEmb (AlgebraicClosure ℚ) jq`, with $j_1 \neq 0$, and over a finite set $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ of places of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` for which there exists a ring homomorphism $j$ from `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` to `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` such that (i) for every $f \in$ `R₀.integers` the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in `R.integers` with `R.residue` of it equal to $j$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and (ii) a place $Q$ belongs to $N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ exactly when there is $s \in W$ with $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, for all $g$.
--
--   On the scheme $\mathfrak{X}_1 =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel ↥A₁ ↥T₁ j₁`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236), the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{XFin} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgFin` (the elements of $T_1$ integral over $A_1[j_1]$) and $\mathrm{XInf} = \operatorname{Spec}$ `chartAlgInf` (those integral over $A_1[j_1^{-1}]$), five predicates are introduced. For $x \in \mathfrak{X}_1$ and $f \in T_1$, `InStalk x f` says that for every point $y$ of $\mathrm{XFin}$ with `ιFin` carrying $y$ to $x$ there are $g, h$ in `chartAlgFin` with $h \notin y$ and $f h = g$ in $T_1$, and likewise for every point of $\mathrm{XInf}$ over $x$ with `chartAlgInf`; `InMax x f` is the same with the additional requirement $g \in y$ in both clauses. For a place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, `Centred P x` says that $P$ is rational and that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in the valuation subring of $P$, has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and satisfies $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ less than $1$ if and only if `InMax x f`. The predicate `GoodPt x` is the conjunction of: `toBase` carries $x$ to the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A_1$; every $y$ with $x \rightsquigarrow y$ equals $x$; for every point $y$ of $\mathrm{XFin}$ over $x$, every $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of `R.integers` lies in $y$, and the same for $\mathrm{XInf}$ and `chartAlgInf`; and for every point $y$ of $\mathrm{XFin}$ over $x$, every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi$ from `chartAlgFin` to $\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j_1)$ on the chart coordinate `jChartFin` avoids [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7). The predicate `Reads x Q` says that every $f$ with `InStalk x f` lies in `R.integers`, has `R.residue` of it in the valuation subring of $Q$, and that this residue is a non-unit of that valuation subring exactly when `InMax x f`. The predicate `OffBranch x` says that for every line $\ell \neq \mathrm{lineInfty}\,q$ and every point $y$ of $\mathrm{XFin}$ over $x$ there is $b \in$ `chartAlgFin` whose image in `fieldBar q M'` is a non-unit of $O_{\mathrm{Ig}}(\ell)$ with $b \notin y$, and correspondingly for $\mathrm{XInf}$ and `chartAlgInf`.
--
--   The assertion is: for every place $Q$ of `xHFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) (q ^ 2 * M') (levelH q M')` with $Q \notin N_{\mathrm{Ig}}$ there exists a point $x$ of $\mathfrak{X}_1$ such that `GoodPt x`, `OffBranch x` and `Reads x Q` all hold. The abbreviation `Centred` is introduced alongside the others but does not occur in this conclusion.
--
--   This is the existence half of the centring analysis for the two-chart integral model of the full-level modular curve over a henselian discrete valuation base: every place of the reduced Igusa function field that is not one of the supersingular node places is read off at a closed point of the special fibre which lies on the $\infty$-Igusa branch only and whose $j$-invariant is not supersingular. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.reads_unique_and_exists_offBranch_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel), which adds uniqueness of the point reading a given place, and it rests on [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_special_closed_branch_reads_of_isRational_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_special_closed_branch_reads_of_isRational_twoChartIntegralModel), [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.not_mem_ssJSet_of_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.not_mem_ssJSet_of_reads_of_not_mem_igusaNodes_twoChartIntegralModel) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.offBranch_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.offBranch_of_goodPt_twoChartIntegralModel).
